# RPI Touch HMI (720x720)

A touch-friendly Raspberry Pi HMI for controlling four relays from a 720x720 touchscreen.

## Features

- clean 720x720 GUI layout with four large touch buttons in a 2x2 grid
- explicit relay state tracking so ON/OFF toggling is reliable
- active-low and active-high support via `ACTIVE_LOW`
- safe shutdown by turning all relays off before GPIO cleanup

## Hardware

- Raspberry Pi
- 720x720 touch display
- 4-channel relay board

## GPIO mapping

- Relay 1 -> GPIO17
- Relay 2 -> GPIO27
- Relay 3 -> GPIO22
- Relay 4 -> GPIO23

## Installation

```bash
cd ~/RPI_Touch_HMI
python3 -m venv ~/hmi-venv
source ~/hmi-venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install kivy RPi.GPIO
```

## Run manually

```bash
source ~/hmi-venv/bin/activate
python main.py
```

## Run unit tests

```bash
source ~/hmi-venv/bin/activate
python -m unittest discover -s tests
```

## Systemd autostart

```bash
sudo cp hmi.service /etc/systemd/system/hmi.service
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable hmi.service
sudo systemctl start hmi.service
```

If your relay board is active-high instead of active-low, set `ACTIVE_LOW = False` in `main.py`.
